  "Question": "The first side of a triangle is \\((3a+2)\\) cm long. The second side is \\((a-1)\\) cm longer than the first, and the third side is 3 cm shorter than the second. The perimeter simplifies to \\(pa+q\\), where \\(p\\) and \\(q\\) are constants. Find the value of \\(p+q\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "12",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The second side is \\(3a+2+a-1=4a+1\\), and the third side is \\(4a+1-3=4a-2\\). The perimeter is \\((3a+2)+(4a+1)+(4a-2)=11a+1\\), so \\(p+q=12\\).",
